From: WPE4YDPv2 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: do not gate audio-only playback on a video sample

Cloud gaming pages can attach the same MediaStream to separate audio and video
elements. The audio element intentionally excludes the video track, but
receivedAudioSampleBeforeVideo() still inspects the parent stream's complete
track list and drops every audio sample until a video sample arrives in that
audio-only pipeline. That video sample can never arrive, so playbin remains
paused and no platform audio sink is opened.

Apply the audio-before-video synchronization only to a video consumer. A pure
audio consumer can preroll and play immediately. Video consumers retain the
existing first-video-sample ordering protection.

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
@@ -1039,6 +1039,9 @@ bool InternalSource::receivedAudioSampleBeforeVideo()
 {
     auto src = WEBKIT_MEDIA_STREAM_SRC_CAST(m_parent);
 
+    if (!m_consumerIsVideoPlayer)
+        return false;
+
     if (m_consumerIsVideoPlayer && m_track && m_track->source().isIncomingAudioSource()
         && allowIncomingPlayerAudioBeforeVideo())
         return false;
